var documenterSearchIndex = {"docs":
[{"category":"section","location":"api/#API-Reference","page":"API","text":"","title":"API Reference"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#EnergyFlow.CustomMetric","page":"API","text":"User provides a distance function f(viewofcoords0coli, viewofcoords1colj) -> scalar distance. R and beta are applied: final_cost = (f(a,b) / R)^β\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow.CustomMetric"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#EnergyFlow.EMDWorkspace","page":"API","text":"EMDWorkspace{V}\n\nPre-allocated workspace for repeated EMD computations. Avoids re-allocation when computing many EMDs of similar sizes.\n\nFields\n\nns: NetworkSimplex solver workspace\nbeta, R: EMD parameters\nnorm: if true, normalize weights before solving\nparallel_threshold: use parallel cost fill when n0real * n1real >= this value (default 40_000)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow.EMDWorkspace"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EnergyFlow.EMDWorkspace-Union{Tuple{Int64, Int64}, Tuple{V}} where V","page":"API","text":"EMDWorkspace{V}(max_n0, max_n1; beta=1.0, R=1.0, norm=true)\n\nCreate a workspace for computing EMD between distributions of up to maxn0 and maxn1 particles.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow.EMDWorkspace"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#EnergyFlow.EtaPhiMetric","page":"API","text":"Eta-Phi with phi periodicity: cost = (sqrt(Δη² + Δφwrap²) / R)^β where Δφwrap = π - |mod(|Δφ|, 2π) - π|. Assumes coords dim 1 = η (rapidity/pseudorapidity), dim 2 = φ (azimuthal angle).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow.EtaPhiMetric"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#EnergyFlow.EuclideanMetric","page":"API","text":"Default: Euclidean distance. cost = (sqrt(Σ(Δx_k²)) / R)^β\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow.EuclideanMetric"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#EnergyFlow.NetworkSimplexSolver","page":"API","text":"NetworkSimplexSolver{V}\n\nPre-allocated workspace for network simplex on a complete bipartite graph. All arrays are allocated once for the maximum problem size; no hot-path allocation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow.NetworkSimplexSolver"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#EnergyFlow.PrecomputedMetric","page":"API","text":"User provides a precomputed n0×n1 cost matrix directly. Values are used as-is (R and beta are NOT applied).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow.PrecomputedMetric"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#EnergyFlow.SinkhornWorkspace","page":"API","text":"SinkhornWorkspace{V<:AbstractFloat}\n\nPre-allocated workspace for Sinkhorn OT computation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow.SinkhornWorkspace"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#EnergyFlow.SquaredEuclideanMetric","page":"API","text":"Squared Euclidean: cost = (Σ(Δx_k²))^β / R^β (no sqrt). Equivalent to EuclideanMetric for β=2 when R is the same.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow.SquaredEuclideanMetric"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EnergyFlow._emd_raw!-Union{Tuple{V}, Tuple{EMDWorkspace{V}, AbstractVector{V}, AbstractMatrix{V}, AbstractVector{V}, AbstractMatrix{V}}} where V","page":"API","text":"_emd_raw!(ws, weights0, coords0, weights1, coords1; max_iter=100_000) -> (V, Symbol)\n\nInternal: compute EMD between two distributions using pre-allocated workspace. Takes raw weights and coordinates. Returns (emd_value, status).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow._emd_raw!"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EnergyFlow._emd_raw_alloc-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:Real}, AbstractMatrix{<:Real}, AbstractVector{<:Real}, AbstractMatrix{<:Real}}","page":"API","text":"_emd_raw_alloc(weights0, coords0, weights1, coords1; kwargs...) -> (V, Symbol)\n\nConvenience raw EMD that allocates a workspace internally.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow._emd_raw_alloc"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EnergyFlow._emd_sinkhorn_raw!-Union{Tuple{V}, Tuple{SinkhornWorkspace{V}, AbstractVector{V}, AbstractMatrix{V}, AbstractVector{V}, AbstractMatrix{V}}} where V","page":"API","text":"_emd_sinkhorn_raw!(ws, weights0, coords0, weights1, coords1) -> (V, Symbol)\n\nCompute EMD between two distributions using Sinkhorn with pre-allocated workspace. Handles weight normalization and fictitious particles (for unbalanced case).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow._emd_sinkhorn_raw!"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EnergyFlow._fill_costs!-Union{Tuple{V}, Tuple{EMDWorkspace{V}, EuclideanMetric, AbstractMatrix{V}, AbstractMatrix{V}, Int64, Int64, Bool, Bool}} where V","page":"API","text":"_fill_costs!(ws, metric, coords0, coords1, n0, n1, has_fict_source, has_fict_target)\n\nFill the cost matrix in the NetworkSimplex solver (serial). Dispatches on the metric type.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow._fill_costs!"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EnergyFlow._fill_costs_chunk!-Union{Tuple{V}, Tuple{EuclideanMetric, Vector{V}, AbstractMatrix{V}, AbstractMatrix{V}, Int64, Int64, Int64, Int64, Int64, V, V, V}} where V","page":"API","text":"_fill_costs_chunk!(costs, coords0, coords1, i_start, i_end, n1_eff, n1_real, dim, beta, R, R2)\n\nFill a contiguous chunk of source rows i_start:i_end in the cost matrix (Euclidean). Used as the per-thread body of _fill_costs_parallel!. Arguments are passed explicitly to avoid closure-capture issues in Julia 1.12.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow._fill_costs_chunk!"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EnergyFlow._fill_costs_parallel!-Union{Tuple{V}, Tuple{EMDWorkspace{V}, Union{EtaPhiMetric, EuclideanMetric, SquaredEuclideanMetric}, AbstractMatrix{V}, AbstractMatrix{V}, Int64, Int64, Bool, Bool}} where V","page":"API","text":"_fill_costs_parallel!(ws, metric, coords0, coords1, n0_eff, n1_eff, has_fict_source, has_fict_target)\n\nParallel version of _fill_costs!. Parallelizes over source particles. For PrecomputedMetric and CustomMetric, falls back to serial.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow._fill_costs_parallel!"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EnergyFlow._flat_to_pair-Tuple{Int64, Int64}","page":"API","text":"Map flat upper-triangular index k (1-based) to (i, j) pair with i < j. Uses the SciPy pdist convention.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow._flat_to_pair"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EnergyFlow._pairwise_emd_cross-Union{Tuple{V}, Tuple{Type{V}, AbstractVector{<:Tuple{var\"#s27\", var\"#s26\"} where {var\"#s27\"<:(AbstractVector), var\"#s26\"<:(AbstractMatrix)}}, AbstractVector{<:Tuple{var\"#s24\", var\"#s23\"} where {var\"#s24\"<:(AbstractVector), var\"#s23\"<:(AbstractMatrix)}}}} where V<:AbstractFloat","page":"API","text":"Cross-pairwise EMD: full m x n matrix.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow._pairwise_emd_cross"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EnergyFlow._pairwise_emd_self!-Union{Tuple{V}, Tuple{AbstractVector{V}, AbstractVector{<:Tuple{var\"#s36\", var\"#s35\"} where {var\"#s36\"<:(AbstractVector), var\"#s35\"<:(AbstractMatrix)}}}} where V","page":"API","text":"In-place self-pairwise: writes to pre-allocated results vector.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow._pairwise_emd_self!"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EnergyFlow._pairwise_emd_self-Union{Tuple{V}, Tuple{Type{V}, AbstractVector{<:Tuple{var\"#s33\", var\"#s32\"} where {var\"#s33\"<:(AbstractVector), var\"#s32\"<:(AbstractMatrix)}}}} where V<:AbstractFloat","page":"API","text":"Self-pairwise EMD: upper triangular of n x n (n*(n-1)/2 computations).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow._pairwise_emd_self"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EnergyFlow._sinkhorn_annealing!-Union{Tuple{V}, Tuple{SinkhornWorkspace{V}, Int64, Int64, V}} where V","page":"API","text":"_sinkhorn_annealing!(ws, n0, n1, target_eps) -> (cost, status)\n\nRun Sinkhorn with ε-annealing: start from a large ε and geometrically decrease to target_eps, warm-starting each stage from the previous solution.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow._sinkhorn_annealing!"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EnergyFlow._sinkhorn_log_domain!-Union{Tuple{V}, Tuple{SinkhornWorkspace{V}, Int64, Int64, V}} where V","page":"API","text":"_sinkhorn_log_domain!(ws, n0, n1, epsilon) -> (cost, status)\n\nLog-domain Sinkhorn iterations for a single epsilon value. Weights must already be in ws.source_weights and ws.target_weights. Cost matrix must already be filled in ws.C[1:n0, 1:n1]. ws.log_u / ws.log_v must be initialized by the caller (zero or warm-start).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow._sinkhorn_log_domain!"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EnergyFlow._unpack_event-Union{Tuple{V}, Tuple{Type{V}, AbstractMatrix{<:Real}, Union{Nothing, Int64}}} where V<:AbstractFloat","page":"API","text":"_unpack_event(::Type{V}, ev, gdim) -> (weights::Vector{V}, coords::Matrix{V})\n\nExtract weights and coordinates from an EnergyFlow-format event matrix, converting to element type V.\n\nev is an M×(1+d) matrix: column 1 is weights, columns 2:(1+d) are coords. If gdim is not nothing, only the first gdim coordinate columns are used. Returns coords as a dim×M matrix (column-major, one column per particle).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow._unpack_event"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EnergyFlow.emd!-Tuple{EMDWorkspace, AbstractMatrix{<:Real}, AbstractMatrix{<:Real}}","page":"API","text":"emd!(ws, ev0, ev1; backend=get_backend(), gdim=nothing, n_iter_max=100_000) -> Float64\n\nCompute EMD between two events using pre-allocated workspace ws. Dispatches to the active backend.\n\nArguments\n\nws::EMDWorkspace: pre-allocated workspace (beta, R, norm are read from ws).\nev0, ev1: EnergyFlow-format event matrices (M×(1+gdim)).\nbackend: backend to use (default: current global backend).\ngdim: coordinate dimensions to use (nothing = all).\nn_iter_max: max iterations for iterative solvers.\n\nReturns\n\nFloat64 EMD value.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow.emd!"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EnergyFlow.emd-Tuple{AbstractMatrix{<:Real}, AbstractMatrix{<:Real}}","page":"API","text":"emd(ev0, ev1; backend=get_backend(), R=1.0, beta=1.0, norm=false,\n    gdim=nothing, n_iter_max=100_000) -> Float64\n\nCompute EMD between two events. Allocates a fresh workspace. For repeated calls, prefer emd! with a pre-allocated workspace.\n\nArguments\n\nev0, ev1: M×(1+gdim) event matrices.\nbackend: backend to use (default: current global backend).\nR, beta, norm: EMD parameters.\ngdim, n_iter_max: see emd!.\n\nReturns\n\nFloat64 EMD value.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow.emd"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EnergyFlow.emd_ns32!-Tuple{EMDWorkspace{Float32}, AbstractMatrix{<:Real}, AbstractMatrix{<:Real}}","page":"API","text":"emd_ns32!(ws, ev0, ev1; gdim=nothing, n_iter_max=100_000) -> Float32\n\nCompute EMD using the Network Simplex Float32 backend with a pre-allocated EMDWorkspace{Float32}.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow.emd_ns32!"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EnergyFlow.emd_ns32-Tuple{AbstractMatrix{<:Real}, AbstractMatrix{<:Real}}","page":"API","text":"emd_ns32(ev0, ev1; R=1.0, beta=1.0, norm=false, gdim=nothing, n_iter_max=100_000) -> Float32\n\nCompute EMD using the Network Simplex Float32 backend. Allocates a fresh workspace each call. For repeated calls, prefer emd_ns32!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow.emd_ns32"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EnergyFlow.emd_ns64!-Union{Tuple{V}, Tuple{EMDWorkspace{V}, AbstractMatrix{<:Real}, AbstractMatrix{<:Real}}} where V","page":"API","text":"emd_ns64!(ws, ev0, ev1; gdim=nothing, n_iter_max=100_000) -> Float64\n\nCompute EMD using the Network Simplex Float64 backend with a pre-allocated EMDWorkspace. The workspace's beta, R, norm settings are used.\n\nArguments\n\nws::EMDWorkspace: pre-allocated workspace.\nev0, ev1: EnergyFlow-format event matrices (M×(1+gdim)). Column 1 = particle weights (pT); columns 2:(1+gdim) = coordinates.\ngdim: coordinate dimensions to use (nothing = all).\nn_iter_max: max network-simplex iterations.\n\nReturns\n\nFloat64 EMD value.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow.emd_ns64!"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EnergyFlow.emd_ns64-Tuple{AbstractMatrix{<:Real}, AbstractMatrix{<:Real}}","page":"API","text":"emd_ns64(ev0, ev1; R=1.0, beta=1.0, norm=false, gdim=nothing, n_iter_max=100_000) -> Float64\n\nCompute EMD using the Network Simplex Float64 backend. Allocates a fresh workspace each call. For repeated calls, prefer emd_ns64!.\n\nArguments\n\nev0, ev1: M×(1+gdim) matrices. Column 1 = particle weights (pT); columns 2:(1+gdim) = spatial coordinates.\nR: distance scale parameter (default 1.0).\nbeta: distance exponent (default 1.0).\nnorm: normalize weights to sum to 1 before solving (default false).\ngdim: number of coordinate dimensions to use. nothing = use all remaining columns.\nn_iter_max: max network-simplex iterations (default 100_000).\n\nReturns\n\nFloat64 EMD value.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow.emd_ns64"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EnergyFlow.emd_ot32!-Tuple{EMDWorkspace{Float32}, AbstractMatrix{<:Real}, AbstractMatrix{<:Real}}","page":"API","text":"emd_ot32!(ws, ev0, ev1; gdim=nothing, n_iter_max=100_000) -> Float32\n\nCompute EMD using the OT-style Float32 backend (arc mixing enabled).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow.emd_ot32!"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EnergyFlow.emd_ot32-Tuple{AbstractMatrix{<:Real}, AbstractMatrix{<:Real}}","page":"API","text":"emd_ot32(ev0, ev1; R=1.0, beta=1.0, norm=false, gdim=nothing, n_iter_max=100_000) -> Float32\n\nCompute EMD using the OT-style Float32 backend (arc mixing enabled). Allocates a fresh workspace each call. For repeated calls, prefer emd_ot32!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow.emd_ot32"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EnergyFlow.emd_ot64!-Union{Tuple{V}, Tuple{EMDWorkspace{V}, AbstractMatrix{<:Real}, AbstractMatrix{<:Real}}} where V","page":"API","text":"emd_ot64!(ws, ev0, ev1; gdim=nothing, n_iter_max=100_000) -> Float64\n\nCompute EMD using the OT-style Float64 backend (arc mixing enabled). Uses the same NetworkSimplex solver but with POT-style arc interleaving for improved performance on unbalanced transport problems.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow.emd_ot64!"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EnergyFlow.emd_ot64-Tuple{AbstractMatrix{<:Real}, AbstractMatrix{<:Real}}","page":"API","text":"emd_ot64(ev0, ev1; R=1.0, beta=1.0, norm=false, gdim=nothing, n_iter_max=100_000) -> Float64\n\nCompute EMD using the OT-style Float64 backend (arc mixing enabled). Allocates a fresh workspace each call. For repeated calls, prefer emd_ot64!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow.emd_ot64"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EnergyFlow.emd_sinkhorn!-Union{Tuple{V}, Tuple{SinkhornWorkspace{V}, AbstractMatrix{<:Real}, AbstractMatrix{<:Real}}} where V","page":"API","text":"emd_sinkhorn!(ws::SinkhornWorkspace, ev0, ev1; gdim=nothing) -> Float64\n\nCompute approximate EMD using Sinkhorn with a pre-allocated workspace.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow.emd_sinkhorn!"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EnergyFlow.emd_sinkhorn-Tuple{AbstractMatrix{<:Real}, AbstractMatrix{<:Real}}","page":"API","text":"emd_sinkhorn(ev0, ev1; R=1.0, beta=1.0, norm=false, gdim=nothing,\n             epsilon=0.01, max_iter_sinkhorn=5000, sinkhorn_tol=1e-9,\n             annealing=true) -> Float64\n\nCompute approximate EMD using Sinkhorn. Allocates a fresh workspace.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow.emd_sinkhorn"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#EnergyFlow.emds","page":"API","text":"emds(events0, events1=nothing; backend=get_backend(), R=1.0, beta=1.0,\n     norm=false, gdim=nothing, n_iter_max=100_000)\n\nCompute pairwise EMDs. Dispatches to the active backend.\n\nReturns\n\nSelf-pairwise (events1=nothing): Vector{Float64} of length n*(n-1)/2.\nCross-pairwise: Matrix{Float64} of shape (length(events0), length(events1)).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow.emds"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EnergyFlow.emds!-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:AbstractFloat}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractMatrix{<:Real}}}","page":"API","text":"emds!(results, events0; backend=get_backend(), R=1.0, beta=1.0, norm=false,\n      gdim=nothing, n_iter_max=100_000)\n\nIn-place self-pairwise EMD: writes to pre-allocated results vector (flat upper-triangular, length n*(n-1)/2). Dispatches to the active backend.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow.emds!"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#EnergyFlow.emds_ns32","page":"API","text":"emds_ns32(events0, events1=nothing; R=1.0, beta=1.0, norm=false, gdim=nothing,\n          n_iter_max=100_000)\n\nPairwise EMDs using the Network Simplex Float32 backend. Returns Vector{Float32} (self) or Matrix{Float32} (cross).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow.emds_ns32"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EnergyFlow.emds_ns32!-Tuple{AbstractVector{Float32}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractMatrix{<:Real}}}","page":"API","text":"emds_ns32!(results, events0; R=1.0, beta=1.0, norm=false, gdim=nothing,\n           n_iter_max=100_000)\n\nIn-place pairwise EMDs using the Network Simplex Float32 backend.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow.emds_ns32!"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#EnergyFlow.emds_ns64","page":"API","text":"emds_ns64(events0, events1=nothing; R=1.0, beta=1.0, norm=false, gdim=nothing,\n          n_iter_max=100_000)\n\nCompute pairwise EMDs using the Network Simplex Float64 backend.\n\nArguments\n\nevents0: Vector of event matrices (each M x (1+gdim)).\nevents1: nothing for self-pairwise, or a second Vector of events for cross-pairwise.\nR, beta, norm, gdim, n_iter_max: same as emd_ns64.\n\nReturns\n\nSelf-pairwise (events1=nothing): Vector{Float64} of length n*(n-1)/2 in SciPy pdist (upper-triangular row-major) order.\nCross-pairwise: Matrix{Float64} of shape (length(events0), length(events1)).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow.emds_ns64"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EnergyFlow.emds_ns64!-Tuple{AbstractVector{Float64}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractMatrix{<:Real}}}","page":"API","text":"emds_ns64!(results, events0; R=1.0, beta=1.0, norm=false, gdim=nothing,\n           n_iter_max=100_000)\n\nIn-place version: writes pairwise EMD values to pre-allocated results vector (flat upper-triangular, length n*(n-1)/2).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow.emds_ns64!"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#EnergyFlow.emds_ot32","page":"API","text":"emds_ot32(events0, events1=nothing; R=1.0, beta=1.0, norm=false, gdim=nothing,\n          n_iter_max=100_000)\n\nPairwise EMDs using the OT-style Float32 backend (arc mixing enabled).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow.emds_ot32"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EnergyFlow.emds_ot32!-Tuple{AbstractVector{Float32}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractMatrix{<:Real}}}","page":"API","text":"emds_ot32!(results, events0; R=1.0, beta=1.0, norm=false, gdim=nothing,\n           n_iter_max=100_000)\n\nIn-place pairwise EMDs using the OT-style Float32 backend (arc mixing enabled).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow.emds_ot32!"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#EnergyFlow.emds_ot64","page":"API","text":"emds_ot64(events0, events1=nothing; R=1.0, beta=1.0, norm=false, gdim=nothing,\n          n_iter_max=100_000)\n\nPairwise EMDs using the OT-style Float64 backend (arc mixing enabled). See emds_ns64 for argument documentation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow.emds_ot64"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EnergyFlow.emds_ot64!-Tuple{AbstractVector{Float64}, AbstractVector{<:AbstractMatrix{<:Real}}}","page":"API","text":"emds_ot64!(results, events0; R=1.0, beta=1.0, norm=false, gdim=nothing,\n           n_iter_max=100_000)\n\nIn-place pairwise EMDs using the OT-style Float64 backend (arc mixing enabled). See emds_ns64! for argument documentation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow.emds_ot64!"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#EnergyFlow.emds_sinkhorn","page":"API","text":"emds_sinkhorn(events0, events1=nothing; R=1.0, beta=1.0, norm=false,\n              gdim=nothing, epsilon=0.01, max_iter_sinkhorn=5000,\n              sinkhorn_tol=1e-9, annealing=true) -> Vector or Matrix\n\nPairwise EMDs using the Sinkhorn backend.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow.emds_sinkhorn"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EnergyFlow.get_backend-Tuple{}","page":"API","text":"get_backend() -> Symbol\n\nReturn the current default EMD backend.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow.get_backend"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EnergyFlow.load_hepmc3_events-Tuple{String}","page":"API","text":"load_hepmc3_events(filepath; maxevents=-1, skipevents=0, status=1, min_pt=0.0)\n    -> Vector{Matrix{Float64}}\n\nLoad events from a HepMC3 ASCII file and convert to EnergyFlow event matrices. Each event is an M×3 Matrix{Float64} with columns [pT, η, φ].\n\nOnly final-state particles with the given status code (default 1) are kept. Particles with pT ≤ min_pt (including beam-axis particles with pT = 0) are skipped. This is a standalone parser; it does not require LorentzVectorHEP.\n\nHepMC3 ASCII P-line format\n\nP barcode vertex pdgid px py pz energy mass status [...]\n\nCoordinate conventions\n\npT  = √(px² + py²)          — particle weight\nη   = asinh(pz / pT)        — pseudorapidity\nφ   = atan(py, px) ∈ (-π,π] — azimuthal angle (radians)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow.load_hepmc3_events"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EnergyFlow.network_simplex!-Union{Tuple{V}, Tuple{NetworkSimplexSolver{V}, AbstractVector{V}, AbstractVector{V}}} where V","page":"API","text":"network_simplex!(ns, source_weights, target_weights; max_iter) -> Symbol\n\nSolve the min-cost transportation problem. Costs must be set in ns.costs[1:n0*n1]. Returns status: :optimal, :infeasible, :unbounded, :supplymismatch, :maxiter.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow.network_simplex!"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EnergyFlow.set_backend-Tuple{Symbol}","page":"API","text":"set_backend(backend::Symbol)\n\nSet the default EMD backend. Available: :ns64, :ot64, :ns32, :ot32, :sinkhorn.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EnergyFlow.set_backend"},{"category":"section","location":"man/backends_and_metrics/#Backends-and-Metrics","page":"Backends and Metrics","text":"","title":"Backends and Metrics"},{"category":"section","location":"man/backends_and_metrics/#Solver-Backends","page":"Backends and Metrics","text":"EnergyFlow.jl supports exact network-simplex-style solvers and an approximate Sinkhorn solver.\n\nBackend Description\n:ns64 Network simplex, Float64 (default)\n:ot64 Arc-mixing style network simplex, Float64\n:ns32 Network simplex, Float32\n:ot32 Arc-mixing style network simplex, Float32\n:sinkhorn Entropic OT (approximate)\n\nSelect backend per-call:\n\nval = emd(e1, e2; backend=:ot64)\n\nOr set a global default:\n\nset_backend(:ns32)","title":"Solver Backends"},{"category":"section","location":"man/backends_and_metrics/#Ground-Metrics","page":"Backends and Metrics","text":"Built-in metrics:\n\nEuclideanMetric()\nSquaredEuclideanMetric()\nEtaPhiMetric()\nPrecomputedMetric(cost_matrix)\nCustomMetric(f)\n\nExample:\n\nval = emd(e1, e2; metric=EtaPhiMetric(), R=1.0, beta=1.0)","title":"Ground Metrics"},{"category":"section","location":"man/getting_started/#Getting-Started","page":"Getting Started","text":"","title":"Getting Started"},{"category":"section","location":"man/getting_started/#Basic-Usage","page":"Getting Started","text":"using EnergyFlow\n\nevents = load_hepmc3_events(\"data/sk_example_PU.hepmc\"; maxevents=20)\n\n# Single-pair EMD\nval = emd(events[1], events[2]; R=1.0, beta=1.0, norm=true)\n\n# Cross-pairwise distances (matrix)\nD = emds(events[1:10], events[11:20]; R=1.0, beta=1.0, norm=true)\n\n# Self-pairwise distances (flattened upper triangle)\ndists = emds(events[1:10]; R=1.0, beta=1.0, norm=true)","title":"Basic Usage"},{"category":"section","location":"man/getting_started/#Reusing-Workspaces","page":"Getting Started","text":"For repeated computations, reusing a workspace avoids repeated allocations.\n\nn = maximum(size(e, 1) for e in events)   # largest event\nws = EMDWorkspace(n, n; beta=1.0, R=1.0, norm=true)\nval = emd!(ws, events[1], events[2])","title":"Reusing Workspaces"},{"category":"section","location":"#EnergyFlow.jl","page":"Home","text":"EnergyFlow.jl computes the Energy Mover's Distance (EMD) between collider events with multiple exact and approximate backends.","title":"EnergyFlow.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"#Highlights","page":"Home","text":"Exact solvers with network simplex backends (:ns64, :ot64, :ns32, :ot32)\nApproximate entropic solver (:sinkhorn)\nFlexible ground metrics (EuclideanMetric, SquaredEuclideanMetric, EtaPhiMetric, PrecomputedMetric, CustomMetric)\nSingle-pair and pairwise APIs (emd, emds) plus in-place workspace variants","title":"Highlights"},{"category":"section","location":"#Installation","page":"Home","text":"using Pkg\nPkg.add(\"EnergyFlow\")","title":"Installation"},{"category":"section","location":"#Quick-Start","page":"Home","text":"using EnergyFlow\n\nevents = load_hepmc3_events(\"data/sk_example_PU.hepmc\"; maxevents=20)\n\nval = emd(events[1], events[2]; R=1.0, beta=1.0, norm=true)\nD = emds(events[1:10], events[11:20]; R=1.0, beta=1.0, norm=true)\ndists = emds(events[1:10]; R=1.0, beta=1.0, norm=true)\n\nContinue with the manual or browse the API reference.","title":"Quick Start"}]
}
